<title>SINGAPORE: India sells Cochin naphtha to Glencore at - $16/T.</title>
<headline>India sells Cochin naphtha to Glencore at - $16/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold by tender 30,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting from Cochin to Swiss trader Glencore at $16.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board (fob) basis, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender for the cargo lifting from the east coast between March 1-3 closed February 20 and was valid for one day.</p>
<p>Sources at Glencore were unable to confirm the deal saying they had not yet received confirmation.</p>
<p>Bullish sentiment in North Asia amid tight supplies have pushed up the price of naphtha, traders said.  </p>
<p>The award was much higher than IOC's last HAN export from Cochin, which loaded January 29-31, at a $20.98 discount.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
